==Old English==

===Alternative forms===
* {{l|ang|mear}}, {{l|ang|mearg}}

===Etymology===
From {{inh|ang|gem-pro|*marhaz}}, from {{der|ang|ine-pro|*márkos||horse}}. Cognate with {{cog|ofs|mar||horse}}, {{m|ofs|merie||mare}} ({{cog|fy|merje||mare}}), {{cog|osx|merge}}, {{m|osx|meriha||mare}}, {{cog|nl|merrie||mare}}, {{cog|goh|marah||horse}}, {{m|goh|meriha||mare}} ({{cog|de|Mähre||mare}}), {{cog|non|marr||horse}} ({{cog|is|mar}}), {{m|non|merr||mare}} ({{cog|sv|märr||mare}}), {{cog|got|𐌼𐌰𐍂𐌷𐍃}}. The Indo-European root is also the source of {{cog|ga|marc}} and {{cog|cy|march||horse}}.

===Pronunciation===
